window.FIELD_GUIDE_MODULES["g-tools"] = {"id":"g-tools","title":"Gaming Backend: Suggested Tool Mapping","lessons":[{"title":"Part 1","blocks":[{"h":false,"c":false,"t":"Comprehensive Backend Game Logic Checklist ‍‍ 1. Authentication & Player Identity ●​ User registration / login (email, OAuth, Steam, Discord, etc.)​  ●​ Player profiles & persistent user IDs​  ●​ Token-based authentication (JWT, OAuth2, etc.)​ ⚔️ ●​ Anti-smurf / duplicate account detection​ 2. Matchmaking Logic ●​ Ticket creation, cancellation, expiration​  ●​ Match grouping logic (e.g., ELO, region, party size)​  ●​ Ping/latency-aware placement​  ●​ Lobby assignment and balancing​ ⚖️ ●​ Optional evaluator (for overlapping proposals or fairness metrics)​  ●​ Engagement-based matchmaking (EOMM-like)​ 3. Game Session Management ●​ Game server spin-up & teardown​  ●​ Room/session creation​  ●​ Player join/leave/timeout tracking​ ●​ ⏲ Session timeout or heartbeat mechanism​"},{"h":false,"c":false,"t":"●​ Reconnect/resume logic​ 4. Real-Time State Sync (Optional for Fast-Paced Games) ●​ WebSocket or UDP-based live sync​  ●​ Server-authoritative physics/game logic​ ⚡ ●​ Lag compensation & delta compression​  ●​ Dropout detection and recovery​ 5. Game Rules & State Logic ●​ Level or world management​ ⏳ ●​ Turn timers or session timers​  ●​ Player actions (attacks, movements, interactions)​  ●​ Win/loss/draw resolution​  ●​ Modular rule sets (to support different game modes)​ 6. Persistence & Progression ●​ Player stats (XP, levels, MMR)​  ●​ Inventory systems (items, currency, skins)​  ●​ Achievements / progression tracking​  ●​ Save/load player progress​"},{"h":false,"c":true,"t":" 7. Security & Fairness\n ●​ Anti-cheat validations (movement, packet validation)​  ●​ Rate-limiting / abuse protection​  ●​ Server-side rule enforcement (not client-trust)​  ●​ Monitoring for suspicious behavior (e.g., speed hacks)​\n 8. Social Features\n ●​ Chat (public/private/team)​  ●​ Friends / party system​  ●​ Invitations / notifications​  ●​ Block/report/mute features​\n 9. Match History & Analytics\n️ ●​ Game result logging​  ●​ Player performance summaries​  ●​ Replay systems (event logs, raw states)​  ●​ Backend analytics (e.g., churn, retention, match quality)​\n 10. Operational Features\n ●​ Logging and observability (Prometheus, Grafana, Sentry)​  ●​ Rollbacks / hotfix handling​"},{"h":false,"c":false,"t":"●​ Version control (client-server compatibility)​  ●​ Multi-region deployment and player routing​ ⚙️ ●​ Admin tools for monitoring and moderation​"},{"h":false,"c":true,"t":" Bonus: Infrastructure-Oriented Concerns\n●​ ⛓ Scalability (Kubernetes, server orchestration like Agones/GameLift)​\n ●​ Caching (Redis/Dragonfly for ephemeral states)​  ●​ Message brokers (Pub/Sub, Kafka for scaling comms)​  ●​ Queues (e.g., match processing, game event workers)​  ●​ Fault tolerance and failover​"},{"h":false,"c":false,"t":"Suggested Tool Mapping (based on your stack)"}],"quiz":[{"q":"Authentication & _____ Identity ●​ User registration / login (email, OAuth, Steam, Discord, etc.)​  ●​ Player profiles & persistent user IDs​  ●​ Token-based authentication (JWT, OAuth2, etc.)​ ⚔️ ●​ Anti-smurf / duplicate account detection​ 2.","a":"Player","o":["Game","Player","Logic","Backend"],"why":"From the source text: “Authentication & Player Identity ●​ User registration / login (email, OAuth, Steam, Discord, etc.)​  ●​ Player profiles & persistent user IDs​  ●​ Token-based authentication (JWT, OAuth2, etc.)​ ⚔️ ●​ Anti-smurf / duplicate account detection​ 2.”"},{"q":"_____ Logic ●​ Ticket creation, cancellation, expiration​  ●​ Match grouping logic (e.g., ELO, region, party size)​  ●​ Ping/latency-aware placement​  ●​ Lobby assignment and balancing​ ⚖️ ●​ Optional evaluator (for overlapping proposals or fairness metrics)​  ●​ Engagement-based matchmaking (EOMM-like)​ 3.","a":"Matchmaking","o":["Matchmaking","Token-based","Persistence","Progression"],"why":"From the source text: “Matchmaking Logic ●​ Ticket creation, cancellation, expiration​  ●​ Match grouping logic (e.g., ELO, region, party size)​  ●​ Ping/latency-aware placement​  ●​ Lobby assignment and balancing​ ⚖️ ●​ Optional evaluator (for overlapping proposals or fairness metrics)​  ●​ Engagement-based matchmaking (EOMM-like)​ 3.”"},{"q":"Game _____ Management ●​ Game server spin-up & teardown​  ●​ Room/session creation​  ●​ Player join/leave/timeout tracking​ ●​ ⏲ Session timeout or heartbeat mechanism​","a":"Session","o":["Logic","Backend","Optional","Session"],"why":"From the source text: “Game Session Management ●​ Game server spin-up & teardown​  ●​ Room/session creation​  ●​ Player join/leave/timeout tracking​ ●​ ⏲ Session timeout or heartbeat mechanism​ ●​ Reconnect/resume logic​ 4.”"}]},{"title":"Logic Area","blocks":[{"h":true,"c":false,"t":"Tool Recommendation"},{"h":true,"c":false,"t":"Auth & Session"},{"h":true,"c":false,"t":"NestJS + PostgreSQL/Redis"},{"h":false,"c":false,"t":"Matchmaking"},{"h":true,"c":false,"t":"Open Match or Redwood MMO"},{"h":true,"c":false,"t":"Game State"},{"h":true,"c":false,"t":"WebSocket + Redis for real-time, PG for storage"},{"h":false,"c":false,"t":"Orchestration"},{"h":true,"c":false,"t":"Agones / GameLift / Firebase"},{"h":true,"c":false,"t":"Chat & Social"},{"h":true,"c":false,"t":"Redis pub/sub or Socket.IO"},{"h":true,"c":false,"t":"Analytics & History PostgreSQL, TimescaleDB, or ClickHouse"},{"h":true,"c":false,"t":"Admin Tools"},{"h":true,"c":false,"t":"Custom dashboard in Next.js + NestJS"},{"h":false,"c":true,"t":" Extended & Practical Game Backend Logic Use Cases\n Matchmaking – Advanced Use Cases\n●​ Partial Matches & Waiting Rooms​ ○​ Players may not fully fill a room immediately (e.g., 3/4 players)​ ○​ Temporary holding queue with timeout logic​ ○​ Backfill strategies to auto-fill partial games mid-match​\n●​ Ticket Prioritization​ ○​ Prioritize by:​ ■​ Wait time (longest-waiting first)​ ■​ Skill distance (loosen ELO constraints over time)​ ■​ Player type (e.g., party leaders, streamers)​ ○​ Queue aging with dynamic rules (e.g., “fast lane” queue for VIPs or paid tiers)​\n●​ Conflict Resolution Between Match Proposals​ ○​ Multiple match functions may claim the same player​ ○​ Resolve by:​ ■​ Match score (engagement prediction, fairness)​ ■​ Ticket timestamp (earliest wins)​ ■​ Player preferences (e.g., game mode)​\n●​ Cross-region or Multi-Region Matching​ ○​ Match across regions if latency difference is small​ ○​ Match based on player consent (cross-region allowed)​"},{"h":false,"c":false,"t":"⚖️ Fairness, Anti-Abuse & Behavior Logic ●​ Match Fairness Evaluation​ ○​ Balance team skill averages​ ○​ Account for party size (avoid 4-stacks vs solo)​ ○​ Validate MMR inflation/deflation​ ●​ Behavior Score Integration​ ○​ Match players with similar behavioral histories (toxic vs cooperative)​ ○​ Factor in recent reports, abandon rates, or penalties​ ●​ Abuse Detection​ ○​ Queue dodging or match abandonment tracking​ ○​ Repeated disconnects → temporary suspensions or low-priority queues​ ○​ Smurf detection via IP/device + performance delta​ Game State Handling Edge Cases ●​ Game Resync / State Reconciliation​ ○​ For reconnecting players or in case of desync​ ○​ Store current game state in Redis or memory snapshot​ ○​ Allow client to catch up via event replay or delta sync​ ●​ Rollback Support (in deterministic games)​ ○​ Save historical snapshots​ ○​ Rewind and replay state after detecting inconsistencies or invalid actions​"},{"h":false,"c":false,"t":"●​ Session Expiry and Auto-Win/Forfeit​ ○​ If a team disconnects or fails to act in time → assign default winner​ ○​ Use heartbeats or pings to track presence​ Intelligence and Personalization ●​ Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment (DDA)​ ○​ Adjust enemy AI or match difficulty based on recent player performance​ ●​ Engagement Optimized Matchmaking (EOMM)​ ○​ Predict match outcomes that maximize session retention​ ○​ Use ML or simple rules to suggest \"fun\" over \"fair\"​ ●​ Player Fatigue Models​ ○​ Rotate game modes or opponents to reduce churn from repetitive play​ Inventory, Currency & Economy Handling ●​ Trade & Exchange Validation​ ○​ Validate item trades for fraud or exploit attempts​ ○​ Anti-duplication measures (e.g., lock token on offer)​ ●​ Inventory Transaction Locks​ ○​ Prevent double-spending in rapid actions (e.g., crafting + trade)​ ●​ Daily/Weekly Missions Engine​ ○​ Server-side evaluation of mission progress with reset logic​"},{"h":false,"c":false,"t":"Social & Live Service Events ●​ Seasonal Events / Battle Pass Progression​ ○​ Backend logic to time events, enable/disable content gates​ ○​ Time-based XP multipliers or limited-mode matchmaking​ ●​ Global Chat Rooms or Clan Systems​ ○​ Sharded chat channels using pub/sub or persistent message queues​ ○​ Moderation pipelines for abuse reports​ Bonus: Fault Tolerance & Scaling Scenarios ●​ Dynamic Scaling of Game Servers​ ○​ Spin up/down pods based on real-time player load​ ○​ Use Kubernetes (Agones) or managed GameLift fleets​ ●​ Circuit Breakers for Dependent Services​ ○​ If Redis/DB becomes slow or unreachable → fallback to local memory or queue​ ●​ Graceful Degradation​ ○​ Disable low-priority systems (e.g., cosmetics, social feed) when under load​"}],"quiz":[]}],"stats":{"lessons":2,"questions":3,"blocks":25,"codeBlocks":3}};
